JAVA CALCULATOR — CONCEPTUAL VIVA QUESTIONS
1. ❓ Why did you use a do-while loop?
🎯 What they’re testing:
Do you understand loop behavior.
✅ Answer:
We use a do-while loop because we want the menu to execute at least once before checking the condition. The calculator should first show options, then decide whether to repeat or exit.
2. ❓ Difference between while and do-while loop?
🎯 Testing concept clarity
✅ Answer:
while loop checks condition first, then executes
do-while executes first, then checks condition
So do-while always runs at least once.
3. ❓ Why is switch-case used instead of if-else?
🎯 Decision-making understanding
✅ Answer:
Switch-case is used because it is cleaner and more readable when we have multiple fixed options like 1 to 6. It improves code clarity compared to multiple if-else conditions.
4. ❓ Can we replace switch-case with if-else?
🎯 Flexibility check
✅ Answer:
Yes, we can replace it with if-else ladder, but switch-case is more efficient and easier to read for fixed choices.
5. ❓ Why did you use double instead of int?
🎯 Data type understanding
✅ Answer:
We use double because division can produce decimal values, which cannot be stored accurately in int.
6. ❓ What happens if you divide by zero?
🎯 Error handling awareness
✅ Answer:
Division by zero causes runtime error in integers, but in double it results in infinity or NaN. In this program, we handle it using condition num2 != 0.
7. ❓ What is Scanner class?
🎯 Input handling concept
✅ Answer:
Scanner is a built-in Java class used to take input from the user through keyboard or other input streams.
8. ❓ Why do we use new keyword?
🎯 Object creation concept
✅ Answer:
new keyword is used to create an object in heap memory so that Scanner can be used for input operations.
9. ❓ What is the role of System.in?
🎯 Input stream understanding
✅ Answer:
System.in represents the standard input stream (keyboard input).
10. ❓ What is break used for?
🎯 Loop control
✅ Answer:
break is used to immediately exit the loop when the user selects exit option.
11. ❓ What is modulus operator (%) used for?
🎯 Arithmetic understanding
✅ Answer:
It returns the remainder after division.
Example: 10 % 3 = 1
12. ❓ Why do we close Scanner?
🎯 Resource management
✅ Answer:
We close Scanner using close() to free system resources and avoid memory leaks.
13. ❓ What is default case in switch?
🎯 Error handling
✅ Answer:
Default case runs when user enters an invalid option not defined in any case.
14. ❓ What is entry point of Java program?
🎯 Core Java concept
✅ Answer:
The main method is the entry point where JVM starts program execution.
15. ❓ What is static in main method?
🎯 OOP concept
✅ Answer:
Static means the method belongs to class, so JVM can call it without creating an object.
16. ❓ Why is main method public?
🎯 Access control
✅ Answer:
It is public so that JVM can access it from outside the class.
17. ❓ What happens if we remove main method?
🎯 Execution understanding
✅ Answer:
The program will not run because JVM will not find the starting point.
18. ❓ Can we use multiple main methods?
🎯 Overloading concept
✅ Answer:
Yes, we can overload main method, but JVM will only execute the standard signature.
19. ❓ What is difference between print and println?
🎯 Output concept
✅ Answer:
print() → stays on same line
println() → moves to next line after printing
20. ❓ What is the logic of this program overall?
🎯 Big picture understanding
✅ Answer:
This program is a menu-driven calculator that repeatedly takes user input, performs arithmetic operations using switch-case, and exits when the user selects option 6.
